<title>JAPAN: Kawasaki to form Philippine design unit.</title>
<headline>Kawasaki to form Philippine design unit.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-12-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Kawasaki Heavy Industries Ltd will set up a wholly owned plant-design company in the Philippines in January in a bid to cut the labour costs involved in designing plants in Asia, a Kawasaki spokesman said on Thursday.</p>
<p>The new company, named HKH Design &amp; Technical Service Inc and based in Manila, will be capitalised at 3.5 million pesos, equivalent to 14.45 million yen. It will design plants, mainly for cement production in Asia, the spokesman said.</p>
<p>The new company will hire 30 local engineers, he said.</p>
</text>
